  "aliases": [
    "Lake Mariner Data Campus"
  ],
  "summary": "TeraWulf campus on the site of a retired coal-fired power plant in Barker, New York, that began operating in 2022, has hosted bitcoin mining and is being expanded for high-performance computing for AI. TeraWulf has leased 60 MW of critical IT load to Core42 and about 378 MW to Fluidstack, whose lease obligations carry Google credit support. About 102 MW of HPC capacity was earning revenue after building CB-3 was delivered in July 2026, while CB-4 and CB-5 (336 MW combined) were under construction. TeraWulf cites about 500 MW of near-term gross capacity and potential to reach about 750 MW.",
